From 28aa9dfe31fd67572c7b68db78ecb036172a60d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:47:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Kanban worker node: never replace a copy from a
 replica behind this gateway's push

A sync round pulls the replica first and pushes the live outbox second, so rows this gateway just pushed reach
the replica only with the next round's pull. A dispatcher tick in that window (the gateway runs the sync loop
and the dispatcher concurrently) evicted a ready worker copy (empty outbox, no respawn_guarded recorded yet)
and re-imported it from the replica without those rows. After an out-of-band lease release (`kanban reclaim`,
dashboard reclaim, reassign --reclaim-first) the replica already showed the card ready, so a crashed PR
owner's copy came back without its `Opened <PR>` comment and `reclaimed` event, active_pr did not hold and
the owner was respawned with no handoff (t_01a1cfedbfe95b4f).

kanban_replica_lag records, in the gateway process, which cards the Board acknowledged after the replica's
last completed pull (push -> acked; _pulled_replica -> pull generation). evict keeps a lagging copy the
local guard holds, and pickup does not re-import a lagging card until the replica holds the push. Entries
expire after 120 s, so a replica whose pulls keep failing never pins a copy; a process that never pushed
(CLI dispatch) behaves as before. Held-copy pickup-budget behaviour is unchanged.
